<div class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>This website is operated by JZB4 Studios, a sole trader business (enskild näringsverksamhet) run by Osama Ateeq, Lilla Regementsvägen 10, 415 27 Gothenburg, Sweden. Email: <a href="mailto:contact@jzb4.com">contact@jzb4.com</a>. We are the data controller for the personal data described below.</p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
        <p>When you send us a message we receive your first name, last name, email address, chosen subject and message. We use them only to reply to you. Messages are delivered by email through Zoho Mail and are stored only in our mailbox. They are not saved in the website's database. We keep them for up to 12 months from receipt and then delete them. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).</p>

    <h2>Spam protection and security</h2>
    <p>The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, and the site is delivered through Cloudflare. They process technical data such as your IP address and browser details to protect the site from abuse.</p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>The site runs on Google Cloud servers in the United States. Server logs (IP address, requested page, time) are kept for a short period for security and troubleshooting and are then overwritten.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The site uses only strictly necessary cookies, such as a security token for the contact form. There are no analytics or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Embedded content</h2>
    <p>Game pages embed videos from YouTube (Google) in privacy-enhanced mode and widgets from itch.io, and the Contact page shows a Google Maps map when you click to load it. When these load, your browser contacts those services, which receive your IP address and may set their own cookies. Their own privacy policies apply.</p>

    <h2>Transfers outside the EU</h2>
    <p>Some of the services above (Google, Cloudflare, Zoho and others) are based in or use servers in the United States. They rely on EU-approved transfer mechanisms such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your personal data, or object to how it is used, by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@jzb4.com">contact@jzb4.com</a>. You can also complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY), imy.se.</p>
</div>
